Cell["\<\
The two seasonally varying coefficients used in the toy model. R(t) is \
negative through spring and positive through autumn; \[Sigma]\_w(t) is \
largest in early spring when WWBs are observed to peak.\
\>", "Caption",
 FontFamily->
  "Helvetica",ExpressionUUID->"f89c4d57-4ce9-421d-805e-8915a64ab3d1"],

Cell[BoxData[
 FontSlant -> Italic], "Input",ExpressionUUID->"c533c118-c11e-43f0-b5c5-2d5d5b726ddb"],

Cell[BoxData[
 FontSize -> 11], "Input",ExpressionUUID->"d629ff0e-9ff6-4654-ae92-a62aa4725913"],

Cell["Caption", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"4494fb14-0556-40b0-ba13-f7abeaa37f2d"],

Cell[BoxData[
 CellMargins -> {{60, 60}, {2, 14}}], "Input",ExpressionUUID->"8c04633e-1b01-4d6a-ab46-42d85130425e"],

Cell["\<\
Integrating with Euler\[Dash]Maruyama (dt = 0.05 months) gives a realistic \
ENSO time series \[LongDash] interannual oscillations of \[PlusMinus]2 \
\[Degree]C, irregular in amplitude, period ~3\[Dash]6 years:\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"b395ec80-eb42-4e55-a11d-d75222af0dd6"],

